			"color":"#323",
			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Realistic live-action cinematic film in bright morning light on a white coastal sailing pavilion beside a calm turquoise bay. An elegant 25-year-old East Asian woman with natural skin, refined facial features, long dark hair loosely tied behind her neck, and minimal natural makeup prepares a small white sailing boat. She wears an ivory linen shirt with rolled sleeves, pale-blue wide-leg trousers, and a light tan woven belt. Her appearance remains consistent throughout the shot. The open pavilion has white stone surfaces, pale wooden railings, light canvas, and a clear view of the sparkling sea. The mood is calm, airy, elegant, and uplifting. Preserve physically realistic skin, hair, linen, rope, sailcloth, white stone, pale wood, and seawater.\n\nThe video lasts exactly five seconds and uses one continuous stabilized shot.\n\n[0s-1.2s] Begin with a medium-wide rear-right three-quarter view of the woman standing beside the small white sailing boat. A folded triangular sail rests along the boat's low railing. She gently smooths the front edge of the sail with her left hand while her right hand picks up one beige rope attached to the sail. Her posture is relaxed and graceful. The sea and white pavilion remain clearly visible.\n\n[1.2s-3.2s] She pulls the same rope toward a small metal cleat with one continuous, controlled motion. The sail rises gradually from the railing and begins to unfold. The fabric responds naturally to the sea breeze, forming soft realistic folds. Her hands remain attached to the rope, and the rope stays physically connected to the sail and cleat.\n\n[3.2s-4.3s] The sail catches a gentle gust and opens halfway, creating one smooth wave through the white fabric. The woman steadies the rope with both hands, turns her face slightly toward the sea, and allows a small strand of dark hair to move in the wind. The camera performs one slow, low-amplitude lateral arc of approximately 30 degrees from her rear-right side toward her front-right side, revealing her face, the sail, the white boat, and the bright bay together.\n\n[4.3s-5s] The sail settles into a stable partially opened position. She releases her left hand from the fabric, keeps her right hand lightly on the rope, and looks calmly toward the horizon. Hold the final composition for the last half-second with her face, ivory shirt, pale-blue trousers, sail, boat, white pavilion, and turquoise sea clearly visible.\n\nCamera and transitions: one continuous stabilized shot. Use only one slow low-amplitude lateral arc of approximately 30 degrees at a gentle constant speed. No cuts, dissolves, zoom jumps, whip pans, handheld shake, extreme close-up, or sudden changes in framing.\n\nConstraints: exactly one 25-year-old East Asian woman, one small white sailing boat, one triangular white sail, one beige rope, and one metal cleat. No extra people, duplicate sail, duplicate rope, sail changing color, rope disconnecting, floating objects, impossible wind direction, exaggerated hair movement, distorted hands, extra fingers, clothing changes, subtitles, logos, watermarks, or readable text.\n\noverall_soundscape:\n\nBright open coastal ambience continues throughout. Gentle waves move against the pavilion and the boat, a light sea breeze moves the sailcloth and the woman's linen shirt, and the rope produces a restrained friction sound as it passes through the metal cleat. The sail gives one soft fabric snap when the breeze catches it, synchronized with the visible opening. No dialogue, speech, footsteps, or unrelated sound effects.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n\nSoft, elegant non-diegetic music uses sparse acoustic guitar, warm piano, and a very light sustained string pad at a slow relaxed tempo. The music remains quiet beneath the waves and sail sounds, becomes slightly fuller as the sail opens, and ends with one gentle unresolved chord during the final half-second hold."
